@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Materialize recurring commitments
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
actor "User" as actor
box "Frontend — Saturdaze Angular application" #E0F2FE
 participant "WeekendPage" as page
 participant "WeekendPlanService" as client
end box
box "Backend — Saturdaze API" #D1FADF
 participant "WeekendsController" as controller
end box
box "Backend — Saturdaze Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
 participant "GenerateWeekendCommandHandler\nPlannerInputLoader\nWeekendPlanner" as handler
end box
box "Backend — Saturdaze Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
 database "AppDbContext\nSQL Server" as db
end box
actor -> page : Plan weekend
page -> client : plan(weekendOf)
client -> controller : POST /api/weekends/plan
controller -> handler : GenerateWeekendCommand after authorization
handler -> db : Load owned family, commitments, catalogs, and history
db --> handler : Planning inputs
handler -> handler : Fetch forecast; BuildFixedBlocks for each weekend day
handler -> handler : L2-011 create locked Commitment blocks; fill flexible gaps
handler -> db : Save weekend and blocks
db --> handler : Saved
handler --> controller : WeekendDto
controller --> client : 200 plan
client --> page : WeekendView
note over handler
Regeneration recreates commitments from the profile.
Their IDs and edited profile times can change.
Strict preservation remains a documented gap.
end note
@enduml
